WEBVTT

00:58:28.333 --> 00:58:30.559
was a really eye-opening
and powerful concept.

00:58:30.583 --> 00:58:32.143
I'm just curious, your comments

00:58:32.167 --> 00:58:34.893
on how you see that
play out in the workplace.

00:58:34.917 --> 00:58:37.559
EP: Great, I'm a
cross-cultural psychologist.

00:58:37.583 --> 00:58:41.101
My work was on
how families and individuals

00:58:41.125 --> 00:58:43.518
deal with large cultural changes.

00:58:43.542 --> 00:58:47.226
And this notion of collective
versus individualistic.

00:58:47.250 --> 00:58:52.393
So what it really
influences a lot is this.

00:58:52.417 --> 00:58:55.434
Do you know that person
that does more than others

00:58:55.458 --> 00:58:57.976
because they can do it
better than anybody else?

00:58:58.000 --> 00:58:59.768
But then quietly resents it,

00:58:59.792 --> 00:59:01.768
but then doesn't want anybody to do it